{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1561419-homebrew-nana-of-the-yazata","id":1561419,"title":"[Homebrew] Nana of the Yazata","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-07T09:43:22-07:00","id":1561419,"title":"[Homebrew] Nana of the Yazata","content":"Hi all!<br /> <br /> This is my write-up for the Kushan/Bactrian/Sogdian goddess, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nana_(Bactrian_goddess)\" target=\"_blank\">Nana</a>. She's part of the Yazata since they share the same Iranian cultural sphere.<br /> <br /> <b>Nana, the Goddess of Authority</b><br /> <br /> Also known as:&quot;: &quot;Nanaia, Nana\u0161ao, Nan\u0113, Noneito, Nono<br /> <br /> The Kushan goddess Nana does not consider herself a mere Yazata, just another creation of Ahura Mazda. In her prime, she eclipsed even the Primordial in worship, reigning as the supreme goddess of the Eastern Iranian world across Bactria, Sogdiana, and the Kushan Empire. A fierce advocate for her people, she is the goddess of life, authority, and strength, ensuring her followers flourish in the landscapes of Central Asia. As a four-armed goddess of victory astride a massive lion, she is ever-ready to trample the fields of her enemies. Like Ahura Mazda in the west, Nana was the ultimate bestower of royal authority in the east; she is a true kingmaker, conferring divine glory (khwarenah) upon the greatest of her subjects. Throughout the ages, she has taken many consorts, including Tishtrya and Vayu of the Yazatas, Shiva of the Devas, and Hermes-Mercury of the Theoi.<br /> <br /> Today, Nana is a deity torn between many worlds. Though major world religions have largely overtaken her ancient worship, she maintains secret precincts throughout Central Asia where devoted practitioners continue her ecstatic rites of mourning. When she incarnates in the mortal world, she claims many mantles drawn from her vast transcultural history, including Xiwangmu (the Queen Mother of the West of the Shen), as well as Durga and Uma of the Devas. In her mortal guises, Nana typically assumes roles of immense authority: a corporate kingmaker or a politician with uncanny acumen. Fluid and cultured, she acts as a master diplomat capable of bridging cultural divides. Recently, she has taken the lead in vanquishing Titanspawns wherever they appear, something that the Yazatas view as a potential boon for her formal induction into the pantheon.<br /> <br /> Nana expects her Scions to mirror her multifaceted nature: reaching for glory while serving as the crossroads where knowledge can intersect and prosper. Priding herself on being the ancient nexus of the Silk Road\u2019s many cultures, she raises her Scions to be adaptable, fierce, and cosmopolitan. Chosen from what she deems the absolute best, her Scions are often found working as high-profile activists, elite military commanders, and international diplomats.<br /> <br /> <b>Callings</b>: Leader, Liminal, Warrior<br /> <b>Purviews</b>: Epic Strength, Epic Stamina, Fertility, Health, Prosperity, Stars, War","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Pantheon(s):<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LMQFZLq3NrOHs2cp7OWnfukuHCNI4h_0/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Nat, the Spirits of Myanmar</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1WDvOmQCR3a25WbVowfe8KgGbGLU0yzX3/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Phi, the Spirits of the Tai People</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13670-svarogg","name":"Svarogg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13670_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}